    "impact": "When an observed async function returns an async generator (including StreamingResponse.body_iterator) with capture_output False, the span is never ended, leading to unfinished spans, missing telemetry, and potential memory/exporter buildup.",
    "suggested_fix": "In _ContextPreservedAsyncGeneratorWrapper.__anext__, move self.span.end() outside the if self.capture_output block so the span is always ended when the generator is exhausted. For example:

except StopAsyncIteration:
    if self.capture_output:
        output = self.items
        if self.transform_fn is not None:
            output = self.transform_fn(self.items)
        elif all(isinstance(item, str) for item in self.items):
            output = "".join(self.items)
        self.span.update(output=output)
    self.span.end()
    raise"
  }
